{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533978-a-question-about-a-logical-attribute-of-a-pc","id":1533978,"title":"A question about a logical attribute of a PC","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-10T09:31:56-07:00","id":1533978,"title":"A question about a logical attribute of a PC","content":"Hello everyone! I'm a new player and I have some troubles figuring out what attribute should I count as &quot;PC's logic and reason&quot;. I've read some posts abot these two attributes, but sometimes it contradicted each other, or it was me, who was unable to recognize the correct answer.<br /> <br /> So I want to create a character that is bad at logical thinking, seeng logical connections and overall, at learning and reasoning. So in this case should I set 1 for Wits or 1 for Intelligence?<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28233-aralios","name":"Aralios","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T09:48:42-07:00","id":1533980,"title":"","content":"I would say that Intelligence is the attribute for logic and reason. Intelligence isn't exactly the same thing and being good and logic and reason, you can have not very logical intelligent people and not very intelligent logical people, but they are going to overlap pretty heavily and all role playing attributes are oversimplifications.<br /> <br /> Wits isn't closely related, its about how fast someone reacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T11:18:39-07:00","id":1533986,"title":"","content":"I would keep intelligence and wits at 1 or 2 max for your character that has a hard time thinking logically and maybe even add a low composure rating to boot to add the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T11:40:38-07:00","id":1533988,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your advices! I also think I'll choose a Brujah clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533978-a-question-about-a-logical-attribute-of-a-pc?p=1533986#post1533986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would keep intelligence and wits at 1 or 2</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea to, may be, start with both 1 wits and intelligence, but I don't actually know if it'll be a viable character. Or it can be viable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28233-aralios","user":"Aralios","date":". 04-10-2024, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28233-aralios","name":"Aralios","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T11:42:50-07:00","id":1533989,"title":"","content":"\u0130ntelligence represents scholarly thinking and memory. Wits is wits, fast thinking and cunning. \u0130ntelligence is theoretical, Wits is practical. Of course, things produced by \u0130ntelligence theoretically can be used practically later on, like inventing something. But the distinction still holds. <br /> <br /> Do you need to fix a problem? Roll Wits to fix it on the spot in a quick way, or roll \u0130ntelligence to devise a long-term solution after taking the necessary time to examine the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T11:51:26-07:00","id":1533990,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, wits would be equivalent to perception in this case, how good your character is at perceiving things. Considering your perspective of reason and logic, a character would roll wits + investigation or awareness if he wanted to gather clues in a given location, or if he wanted to understand an individual's reasons he would use wits + empathy or subterfuge depending on the method. Now intelligence would be more like knowledge, and you would use it to see if your character has knowledge in a given area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T14:48:00-07:00","id":1534001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533978-a-question-about-a-logical-attribute-of-a-pc?p=1533990#post1533990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, wits would be equivalent to perception in this case, how good your character is at perceiving things. Considering your perspective of reason and logic, a character would roll wits + investigation or awareness if he wanted to gather clues in a given location, or if he wanted to understand an individual's reasons he would use wits + empathy or subterfuge depending on the method. Now intelligence would be more like knowledge, and you would use it to see if your character has knowledge in a given area.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in VDA20, those are Perception + Investigate (gathering clues), Perception + Empathy (understanding motives and emotions), Perception + Subterfuge (detecting deception) and Perception + Awareness (sensing supernatural phenomena indirectly - rather than through a power) rolls.<br /> Interpreting clues after gathering them could be an Intelligence + Enigmas (or Investigate in V20) roll, while deciphering the sensations one gathered through the Awareness roll to better understand what supernatural phenomenon one is facing would be an Intelligence + Occult roll. <br /> Truth be told, Wits is treated poorly by the game system. It is mostly used for Initiative, to drive vehicles or ride animals (but it can be replaced by Dexterity) and with Survival to cover tracks or find quickly a place to sleep or a means to feed. One may also argue for using Perception + Survival when looking for food or shelter, but I think Wits is better because sometimes it's not only about noticing the presence of something (like the entrance to a cave), but also about getting ideas fast on how to use what is already present and near to provide shelter. Quickly assessing a situation and providing a solution is Wits territory, even if the task involves some perception and thought.<br /> By contrast, Perception and Intelligence are used in many more rolls. I believe Chronicles of Darkness, by getting rid of Perception and folding its functions in Wits, improves the system of mental attributes overall.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28233-aralios\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28233\" data-vbnamecard=\"28233\">Aralios</a>, going back to your question, logic and reasoning are usually two sub-functions of Intelligence in game. My suggestion for your character is to give them Intelligence 1. Wits and Perception, on the other side, may be as low or high as you wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T23:58:22-07:00","id":1534016,"title":"","content":"Thank you everyone! It makes the whole situation clear to me as a novice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28233-aralios","name":"Aralios","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T13:14:47-07:00","id":1534147,"title":"","content":"I hope that all of our answers helped you out with your character and maybe you will give us later an update on how it went.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T11:27:02-07:00","id":1534203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533978-a-question-about-a-logical-attribute-of-a-pc?p=1534147#post1534147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> maybe you will give us later an update on how it went.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you once again! Although we played just about an hour this session, I really enjoyed it and I have a strong feeling that this build would be pretty viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28233-aralios","name":"Aralios","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}